This add-on gives types, routines, for solving the system of equations using
the direct solver UMFPACK from the SuiteSparse library:
https://people.engr.tamu.edu/davis/suitesparse.html

UMFPACK is free software.

This add-on assumes UMFPACK is available and installed.

USAGE::
======

- Build tfem using:

    make all umfpack

  for a usual build + umfpack.

- Use like:

  program myprog

    ...

    use umfpack_m

    ...

    call solve_system_umfpack ( sysmatrix, rhsd, sol )

    ...

  end program myprog

Remarks:
=======

- The matrix must be real unsymmetric. As a result, the routine
  create_sysmatrix_structure must NOT be called with symmetric=.true., even if
  the matrix happens to be symmetric.

- See the type solver_options_umfpack_t in umfpack.f90 to see which non-default
  options can be set. See the userguide of UMFPACK for more info about the
  options.

- By default, 32bit integers are used. To change to 64bit integers, edit
  the root Mdefs.mk as follows:

   1. Change the compiler options such that the default integer type is 64bit
      (8 bytes).
   2. Set the preprocessor option I8 by adding -DI8 to the macro FPPFLAGS.
   3. Make sure you link to an umfpack library with 64bit integer BLAS/Lapack.

  Then do a FULL rebuild of tfem, including all possible extras (libhsl, ...).
